  "appeal_decision": null,
  "description": "Change of use of ground and 1st floors from Class E to 18 flats - 12 x one bedroom/one person (of which 10 are studios) and 6 x one bedroom/ 2 person.\n\nIn accordance with the requirements of the GPDO as set out in Article 3(9A and 9B), the development is fully compliant with the Government's Technical housing standards – nationally described space standard. This includes compliance with internal floor area, bedroom size as well as storage and minimum floor to ceiling height requirements.\n\nThe building benefits from an extant planning permission under ref: 25/00277/FULL for development comprising of external alterations including new window openings and roof lights. The applicant confirms that the windows and roof lights would be installed prior to the occupation of any dwellings proposed by this prior approval application and it is considered that this is capable of being secured through a Grampian condition, if deemed necessary. \n\nIn order to assist the assessment of the application, existing elevations have been submitted together with ‘as consented elevations’, which assume the completion of development under planning permission ref: 25/00277/FULL.\n\nThe existing dwellings, (known as Flats 1-12, 46 Vauxhall Bridge Road) located at 1st - 4th floors with a ground floor entrance and ancillary basement storage, are unaffected by the development and outside the scope of this application.\n",
